The Sure Thing is a 1985 American romantic comedy road film directed by Rob Reiner and
starring John Cusack, Daphne Zuniga, Viveca Lindfors, and Nicollette Sheridan.

13
01:01:45,000 --> 01:01:51,000
The film chronicles the cross-country journey of college students Walter Gibson (Cusack) and Alison Bradbury (Zuniga) as they make
their way from New England to Los Angeles over Christmas break, each in an effort to meet their ideal romantic match.

14
01:06:30,000 --> 01:06:36,000
Written by Steven L.

15
01:11:15,000 --> 01:11:21,000
Bloom and Jonathan Roberts, The Sure Thing marked Reiner's second directorial feature
after This Is Spinal Tap (1984), and Cusack's first major starring role.

16
01:16:00,000 --> 01:16:06,000
Released theatrically in the spring of 1985, The Sure Thing was a box-office success and received mostly favorable reviews from film critics, who commended it for its traditional comedic structure,
with some likening it to a modern version of Frank Capra's It Happened One Night (1934),  though Reiner himself stated that the parallels between the two films were unintentional.

17
01:20:45,000 --> 01:20:51,000
In 2017, the British Film Institute ranked The Sure Thing
among Reiner's top five feature films.

